| [D#m] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
My legs are burning, my lungs are on fire
[B]The road is long and the hill is higher
But I [D#m]can hear them cheering from the stands
The ones who ran before me with their o[C#]pen hands
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Since we are surrounded by [D#m]such a [B]great cloud of witness[C#]es
Let us throw off ev[D#m]ery weight
And let us run with en[B]durance the race set [C#]before us
Fixing our eyes on [D#m]Jesus
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Abra[B]ham and Moses, [C#]Rahab [A#m]at the wall
They didn't see the [D#m]finish but they gave it all
Now the baton's in my hand and the time is now
I'm going [C#]to run this race, I'm going [D#m]to show you how
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Since we are surrounded by such a great [B]cloud of witnesses
Let us [C#]throw off every weight
And let us run with en[B]durance the race set [C#]before us
Fixing our [D#m]eyes on Jesus
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
The pioneer [B]and perfecter of [C#]faith
Who for the joy set before [D#m]him endured the [B]cross
Scorning its [C#]shame
And [A#m]has taken his seat at the [D#m]right hand of the throne of God
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Fixing our eyes on Jesus
Fixing our eyes on Jesus
{end_of_verse}

